# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The model that a simulation keeps for the updates of its tunables
# (D254, #324) and the arrays of its program that no value of a
# tunable enters (D[update-kept-arrays], #328), Inputs/python_update_cost.py, on a GPU: a
# sequence of updates of every kind of tunable against a simulation whose
# updates copy the model of the compile, with every program that is built
# from the kept model also built from a copy and compared
# (MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES), and a number of the kept model that is written
# over.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: env MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES=1 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_update_cost.py updates %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU %t | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES=1 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_update_cost.py loud %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOUD
# RUN: env MDRT_CHECK_KEPT_TUPLES=1 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_update_cost.py array %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ARRAY
# CHECK: GPU Double: 203 states, energies, and derivatives over 22 updates of each tunable alone and of all, between steps, a commit, a refusal, a checkpoint with a run continued from it, and a frame evaluator equal those of a simulation whose updates copy the model of the compile, to the bit; 23 programs built from the kept model, 25 arrays kept and 7 made at each, each compared with one built from a copy
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: 203 states, energies, and derivatives over 22 updates of each tunable alone and of all, between steps, a commit, a refusal, a checkpoint with a run continued from it, and a frame evaluator equal those of a simulation whose updates copy the model of the compile, to the bit; 23 programs built from the kept model, 25 arrays kept and 7 made at each, each compared with one built from a copy
# CHECK: update cost updates GPU passed
# LOUD: GPU: a number of the kept model that was written over is found by the comparison with a build from a copy of the model of the compile, which fails the update and names it; the simulation builds from a copy from then on, with the results of one that was not spoiled
# LOUD: update cost loud GPU passed
# ARRAY: GPU: a number of a kept array that was written over is found by the comparison with a build from a copy of the model of the compile, which fails the update and names it; the simulation builds from a copy from then on, with the results of one that was not spoiled
# ARRAY: update cost array GPU passed
